--- body ---

## Context

The OECD CRS pipeline planned by 0713 stops at 2024. It is needed to compare
execution profiles, but insufficient to track the JETPs in 2026. The programme
must also observe the passage announcement -> project -> approval -> signature
-> disbursement -> physical delivery from reports, registers and project pages
published after 2024.

The author asks for exhaustive coverage of the four JETPs: South Africa,
Indonesia, Viet Nam and Senegal. "Exhaustive" is defined over an explicit
universe of sources: national JETP portal, responsible ministries, IPG
co-leads, donors named in the package, multilateral banks, the power utility
and the official pages of each identified project. Any expected source that is
absent, blocked or unpublished is recorded as such; it is neither silently
replaced nor guessed.

The device is a standalone workpackage in `climate-finance-het`. It does not
grow PR #1322, which remains an editorial handover. The Viet Nam pilot in
`conception/jetp/papier-3-ledger/` provides the initial conventions, but the
four countries must be treated with the same evidence contract.

## Actions

### M1 — healthy, frozen base

1. **0716** — provide the minimal corpus contract, DVC storage and
   reproducible ingestion of the already bounded sources.
2. **0717–0720** — provide the existing country inventories and evidence,
   without making their refresh or the resolution of all identities a blocker.
3. **0832** — publish four frozen inventories by sublayer, without merging
   (delivered). **0834 (M1a)** — the MVP explores the data in three tiers: raw
   documents, structured extraction, reconciled facts; South Africa and Vietnam
   recipe; children 0835–0839.
4. **0833 (M1b)** — add canonical identifiers, common taxonomy and certain
   relations; count unresolved `possible_match` separately.

### Former M2 — live monitoring, after acceptance of M1

Renamed on 2026-09-29 (author's decision, see [[0725]]): the new M2 is an
extraction pipeline; this train is split into M3a (discover and freeze), M3b
(extract, reconcile, publish) and M4 (operations).

5. **0721** (M3b) — reconcile the four ledgers with CRS/IATI and produce the
   cross-cutting checks.
6. **0722** (M3a and M4) — install the skill, the watch and the update rules.
7. **0723** (M3b) — join financial events, assets and physical deliveries.
8. **1140** (M3a: one campaign; M4: weekly cadence) — periodic watch for new
   sources, run by a local agent on padme; any candidate remains unadmitted
   until the author's triage.
9. **1141** (M4) — monthly link-rot check and relaunch of Web Archive
   captures, scheduled on padme.

## Invariants

- CRS 2022-2024 is a retrospective layer; no text presents it as the current
  state of a JETP.
- A ledger line represents a dated financial event, not a whole project. The
  announcement, MoU, approval, signature and disbursement layers are never
  added together.
- The primary source's currency is canonical. A third-party conversion remains
  a cross-check observation excluded from aggregates.
- Two scopes coexist: `jetp_strict` when the source explicitly attaches the
  operation to the JETP; `ipg_energy_extended` for context.
- Raw documents are content-addressed, timestamped and tracked by DVC;
  registers, rules and provenance sidecars stay readable in git.
- No DVC data push from this machine: padme remains the data authority per 0713.
- A press item serves as a lead. An accounting value enters the ledger only
  with a primary source or an explicit `secondary_only` verdict.

## Exit criteria

- [x] M1a / 0834: the MVP explores documents, extractions and facts end to end on the SA and VN recipes; the frozen tables of 0832 are its input
- [ ] M1b / 0833 publishes the bounded catalogue and counts unresolved matches
- [ ] The M1 milestone of 0725 accepts the base before any start of the watch (M3a and M4 since 2026-09-29)
- [ ] The four countries have a bounded source register, a collection
      manifest, a financial ledger and a documented map of absences
- [ ] Every aggregated amount is reconstructible from sourced events
- [ ] Coverage and limits are publishable as method results

Periodic refresh, resolution of `possible_match`, source extension and
finance-asset joins are later criteria (M3 and M4 since 2026-09-29);
they do not block the acceptance of M1.

## Publication programme (13 September 2026)

Tracker 0725 and `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md` reuse this
collection programme for a monthly public observatory and three academic papers.
The short comparison concerns preparation and financing against pre-JETP energy
projects. Physical-delivery work 0723 is an extension, not its prerequisite.
